land-born author describing journeys through Kendal and the northern counties including the Lake country.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The History of the Worthies of England\",\"author\":\"Thomas Fuller\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1662,\"reason\":\"County-by-county survey containing dedicated Cumberland and Westmorland chapters describing the Lake counties' places and worthies.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Description of the County of Westmorland\",\"author\":\"Daniel Fleming\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian survey\",\"year\":1671,\"reason\":\"Sir Daniel Fleming's manuscript topographical description of Westmorland, including the Lake District valleys and fells.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Britannia: or, A Geographical Description of the Kingdoms of England, Scotland, and Ireland, with the Isles and Territories thereto belonging\",\"author\":\"Richard Blome\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1673,\"reason\":\"Chorography with substantial county sections on Cumberland and Westmorland and their lakes and mountains.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Perambulation of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Thomas Denton\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian survey\",\"year\":1688,\"reason\":\"Manuscript antiquarian survey of Cumberland describing the seats, towns and scenery of the Lake District in 1687-88.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Journal or Historical Account of the Life, Travels, Sufferings, Christian Experiences, and Labour of Love in the Work of the Ministry of George Fox\",\"author\":\"George Fox\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1694,\"reason\":\"Recounts Fox's 1652 mission through Westmorland, with sustained narrative of Firbank Fell, Kendal, Underbarrow and Swarthmoor in the Lake counties.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Britannia, Newly Translated into English: With Large Additions and Improvements\",\"author\":\"William Camden; Edmund Gibson (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1695,\"reason\":\"Gibson's edition of Camden's chorography carries detailed descriptions of Cumberland and Westmorland including the Lake mountains.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Miscellany of Poems, Consisting of Original Poems, Translations, Pastorals in the Cumberland Dialect, and Familiar Epistles\",\"author\":\"Josiah Relph\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1747,\"reason\":\"Posthumous collection by the Wigton poet including the earliest substantial verse in Cumberland dialect rooted in the local landscape.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Antiquities of England and Wales\",\"author\":\"Francis Grose\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian\",\"year\":1772,\"reason\":\"Illustrated antiquarian survey with engraved views and descriptions of Cumberland and Westmorland castles, abbeys and monuments including Furness Abbey.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Antiquities of Furness; or, An Account of the Royal Abbey of St. Mary, in the Vale of Nightshade, near Dalton in Furness\",\"author\":\"Thomas West\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian\",\"year\":1774,\"reason\":\"Pioneering account of Furness Abbey and the Furness district at the southern edge of the Lake District, by the author of the first Lakes guidebook.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The History and Antiquities of the Counties of Westmorland and Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Joseph Nicolson; Richard Burn\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"County history\",\"year\":1777,\"reason\":\"The standard eighteenth-century history of the two Lake counties, parish by parish.\"}\n{\"title\":\"An Evening Walk. An Epistle; in Verse. Addressed to a Young Lady, from the Lakes of the North of England\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1793,\"reason\":\"Wordsworth's first published poem, a loco-descriptive walk among the lakes and fells of his native region.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The History of the County of Cumberland, and Some Places Adjacent, from the Earliest Accounts to the Present Time\",\"author\":\"William Hutchinson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"County history\",\"year\":1794,\"reason\":\"Comprehensive history of Cumberland with detailed treatment of the Lake District parishes, by the author of the 1776 Excursion to the Lakes.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Companion and Useful Guide to the Beauties of Scotland, to the Lakes of Westmorland, Cumberland, and Lancashire; and to the Curiosities in the District of Craven\",\"author\":\"Sarah Murray\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Travel writing\",\"year\":1799,\"reason\":\"A woman traveller's guide containing a substantial, self-contained account of touring the English Lakes.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Lyrical Ballads, with Other Poems. In Two Volumes\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth; Samuel Taylor Coleridge\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1800,\"reason\":\"The second volume of the 1800 edition gathers poems set in the Lake District, including Michael, The Brothers and Hart-Leap Well.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Tour through the Northern Counties of England, and the Borders of Scotland\",\"author\":\"Richard Warner\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Travel writing\",\"year\":1802,\"reason\":\"Clergyman's tour containing an extended Lake District itinerary through Cumberland and Westmorland.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Beauties of England and Wales; or, Delineations, Topographical, Historical, and Descriptive, of Each County. Vol. III: Cumberland, the Isle of Man, and Derbyshire\",\"author\":\"John Britton; Edward Wedlake Brayley\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1802,\"reason\":\"The Cumberland section offers a sustained topographical and historical description of the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Ballads in the Cumberland Dialect, Chiefly by R. Anderson\",\"author\":\"Robert Anderson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1805,\"reason\":\"Dialect ballads by the Carlisle-born Cumberland Bard evoking the life and landscape of the Lake county.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Minstrel of the North; or, Cumbrian Legends; Being a Poetical Miscellany of Legendary, Gothic, and Romantic Tales\",\"author\":\"John Stagg\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1810,\"reason\":\"Verse legends drawn from Cumbrian scenery and folklore by the blind bard of Cumberland.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Topographical and Statistical Description of the County of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"George Alexander Cooke\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1810,\"reason\":\"Pocket county topography describing Cumberland's lakes, mountains, towns and antiquities.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Topographical and Statistical Description of the County of Westmorland\",\"author\":\"George Alexander Cooke\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1810,\"reason\":\"Pocket county topography describing Westmorland's Lake District scenery, towns and antiquities.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Bridal of Triermain; or, The Vale of St. John\",\"author\":\"Walter Scott\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1813,\"reason\":\"Romantic narrative poem set in the Vale of St John beneath Skiddaw in the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Poetical Effusions\",\"author\":\"Isabella Lickbarrow\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1814,\"reason\":\"Collection by a Kendal poet including poems on Lake District scenes such as Windermere and the Kent valley.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Excursion, Being a Portion of The Recluse, a Poem\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1814,\"reason\":\"Long philosophical poem set in the Lake District, centred on a Grasmere-like vale and its inhabitants.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Journal of a Tour and Residence in Great Britain, during the Years 1810 and 1811\",\"author\":\"Louis Simond\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Travel writing\",\"year\":1815,\"reason\":\"French-born traveller's account containing a detailed description of his tour through the English Lakes.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Lakes of Lancashire, Westmorland, and Cumberland, Delineated in Forty-Three Engravings from Drawings by Joseph Farington, with Descriptions Historical, Topographical, and Picturesque\",\"author\":\"Thomas Hartwell Horne\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1816,\"reason\":\"Letterpress accompanying Farington's celebrated views, describing each principal Lake District scene after a tour of 1816.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Magna Britannia; Being a Concise Topographical Account of the Several Counties of Great Britain. Volume the Fourth, Containing Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Daniel Lysons; Samuel Lysons\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"County history\",\"year\":1816,\"reason\":\"The Cumberland volume of the Lysons' national topography gives a parish-by-parish account of the Lake county.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Harold the Dauntless: A Poem, in Six Cantos\",\"author\":\"Walter Scott\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1817,\"reason\":\"Verse romance of the Danish settlement laid in Cumberland among the border fells and Inglewood.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Tourist's New Guide: Containing a Description of the Lakes, Mountains, and Scenery in Cumberland, Westmorland, and Lancashire\",\"author\":\"William Green\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Guidebook\",\"year\":1819,\"reason\":\"Ambleside artist's two-volume guide reflecting a lifetime's residence among and study of the Lakes.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Waggoner: A Poem. To which are added, Sonnets\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1819,\"reason\":\"Poem following a waggoner's journey over Dunmail Raise through the heart of the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Confessions of an English Opium-Eater: Being an Extract from the Life of a Scholar\",\"author\":\"Thomas De Quincey\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1821,\"reason\":\"Autobiographical work whose later sections describe the author's life at Dove Cottage, Grasmere, among the Lake poets.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Cumbrian Minstrel: Being a Poetical Miscellany of Legendary, Gothic, and Romantic Tales\",\"author\":\"John Stagg\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1821,\"reason\":\"Further Cumbrian legendary verse by Stagg, steeped in Lake county scenery and superstition.\"}\n{\"title\":\"History, Directory and Gazetteer of the County Palatine of Lancaster\",\"author\":\"Edward Baines\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1824,\"reason\":\"Includes substantial treatment of Furness and Lancashire North of the Sands, the south-western fringe of the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Sir Thomas More: or, Colloquies on the Progress and Prospects of Society\",\"author\":\"Robert Southey\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Essays\",\"year\":1829,\"reason\":\"Dialogues staged around the author's Keswick home beneath Skiddaw, with recurring description of the Lake District landscape.\"}\n{\"title\":\"History, Directory, and Gazetteer, of the Counties of Cumberland and Westmorland, with that Part of the Lake District in Lancashire, Forming the Lordships of Furness and Cartmel\",\"author\":\"William Parson; William White\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1829,\"reason\":\"County directory whose gazetteer describes every Lake District town, valley and lake.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Annals of Kendal: Being a Historical and Descriptive Account of Kendal and its Environs\",\"author\":\"Cornelius Nicholson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1832,\"reason\":\"History of Kendal, the Westmorland market town known as the Gateway to the Lakes, and its surroundings.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Westmorland, Cumberland, Durham, & Northumberland, Illustrated, from Original Drawings by Thomas Allom, George Pickering, &c.\",\"author\":\"Thomas Rose\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1832,\"reason\":\"Illustrated county topography with extensive letterpress on Lake District scenery.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Poems\",\"author\":\"Hartley Coleridge\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1833,\"reason\":\"Collection by Coleridge's son, a lifelong dweller in Grasmere and Rydal, containing sonnets on Lake District places and people.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Recollections of the Lakes and the Lake Poets\",\"author\":\"Thomas De Quincey\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1834,\"reason\":\"Series of reminiscences of Wordsworth, Coleridge and Southey grounded in Grasmere and Keswick life, serialized in Tait's Magazine from 1834.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Lakes of England\",\"author\":\"George Tattersall\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1836,\"reason\":\"Illustrated work describing the principal English lakes and their scenery for the tourist.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The History and Antiquities of Carlisle, with an Account of the Gentlemen's Seats and Antiquities in the Vicinity\",\"author\":\"Samuel Jefferson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1838,\"reason\":\"History of the Cumberland county town and its district, a standard source for the northern Lake county.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Visits to Remarkable Places, Old Halls, Battle Fields, and Scenes Illustrative of Striking Passages in English History and Poetry\",\"author\":\"William Howitt\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Travel writing\",\"year\":1840,\"reason\":\"Includes a sustained account of a visit to Wordsworth at Rydal Mount and the Lake country.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Black's Picturesque Guide to the English Lakes\",\"author\":\"Adam and Charles Black (pub.)\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Guidebook\",\"year\":1841,\"reason\":\"First edition of Black's celebrated series of Lake District guidebooks.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Recreations of Christopher North\",\"author\":\"John Wilson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Essays\",\"year\":1842,\"reason\":\"Contains essays recording walking expeditions in the Lake District around the author's Windermere home, including Christopher in his Sporting Jacket.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The History and Antiquities of Allerdale Ward, above Derwent, in the County of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Samuel Jefferson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1842,\"reason\":\"Local history of the Cumberland ward containing Keswick, Borrowdale and the heart of the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Poetical Works of Miss Susanna Blamire, 'The Muse of Cumberland'\",\"author\":\"Susanna Blamire; Henry Lonsdale (ed.); Patrick Maxwell (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1842,\"reason\":\"First collected edition of the Cumbrian poet's songs and dialect verse rooted in the Eden valley and Lake county.\"}\n{\"title\":\"An Illustrated Itinerary of the County of Lancaster\",\"author\":\"Cyrus Redding\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1842,\"reason\":\"Itinerary covering the Furness district and the Lake District fringe of Lancashire north of the sands.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Kendal and Windermere Railway: Two Letters Re-printed from the Morning Post\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Pamphlet\",\"year\":1844,\"reason\":\"Wordsworth's celebrated protest against bringing the railway into the heart of the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"History, Gazetteer, and Directory of Cumberland, Comprising a General Survey of the County\",\"author\":\"William Mannix; William Whellan\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1847,\"reason\":\"Mid-Victorian directory with historical and topographical accounts of all the Cumberland Lake parishes.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Homes and Haunts of the Most Eminent British Poets\",\"author\":\"William Howitt\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1847,\"reason\":\"Chapters on Wordsworth, Coleridge and Southey describe their Grasmere, Rydal and Keswick homes and the surrounding Lake scenery.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Worthies of Westmorland; or, Notable Persons Born in that County since the Reformation\",\"author\":\"George Atkinson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1849,\"reason\":\"Biographies of Westmorland worthies prefaced by topographical account of the Lake county.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Life and Correspondence of Robert Southey\",\"author\":\"Charles Cuthbert Southey\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1849,\"reason\":\"Life and letters of the poet laureate centred on his forty years at Greta Hall, Keswick, in the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Prelude; or, Growth of a Poet's Mind: An Autobiographical Poem\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1850,\"reason\":\"Autobiographical poem with celebrated books on the poet's childhood and schooldays at Hawkshead and residence at Grasmere.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Memoirs of William Wordsworth, Poet-Laureate, D.C.L.\",\"author\":\"Christopher Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1851,\"reason\":\"Official memoir by the poet's nephew, documenting his life at Grasmere and Rydal Mount in the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Northmen in Cumberland and Westmorland\",\"author\":\"Robert Ferguson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1856,\"reason\":\"Study of Norse settlement, place-names and dialect in the two Lake counties.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Cumberland and Westmorland, Ancient and Modern: The People, Dialect, Superstitions and Customs\",\"author\":\"Jeremiah Sullivan\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1857,\"reason\":\"Account of the people, dialect and customs of the Lake counties, ancient and modern.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Official Illustrated Guide to the Lancaster and Carlisle, Eden Valley, and Penrith Railways\",\"author\":\"George S. Measom\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Railway guide\",\"year\":1859,\"reason\":\"Railway guide describing the approach to the Lakes over Shap and the branches to Kendal and Windermere.\"}\n{\"title\":\"A Glossary of Words and Phrases of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"William Dickinson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Dialect study\",\"year\":1859,\"reason\":\"Glossary recording the dialect spoken across the Cumberland Lake District, by the author of Cumbriana.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The History and Topography of the Counties of Cumberland and Westmorland, Comprising Their Ancient and Modern History\",\"author\":\"William Whellan\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1860,\"reason\":\"Comprehensive county history and gazetteer describing every Lake District parish, valley and town.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Tales and Legends of the English Lakes\",\"author\":\"Wilson Armistead\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Folklore\",\"year\":1863,\"reason\":\"Collection of legends and traditional tales attached to Lake District places.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Lake Country\",\"author\":\"Elizabeth Lynn Linton\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Travel writing\",\"year\":1864,\"reason\":\"Woman novelist's descriptive tour of the Lakes, illustrated with one hundred engravings by W. J. Linton.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Worthies of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Henry Lonsdale\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1867,\"reason\":\"Six-volume series of lives of eminent Cumbrians, a key source for the intellectual history of the Lake county.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Diary, Reminiscences, and Correspondence of Henry Crabb Robinson\",\"author\":\"Henry Crabb Robinson; Thomas Sadler (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Diary\",\"year\":1869,\"reason\":\"Diaries record repeated visits to the Lakes and friendships with Wordsworth, Coleridge and Southey in their Lake District homes.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Folk-Speech of Cumberland and Some Districts Adjacent; Being Stories and Rhymes in the Dialect of that Border County\",\"author\":\"Alexander Craig Gibson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Dialect study\",\"year\":1869,\"reason\":\"Dialect stories and rhymes of Cumberland by the Coniston-based physician and author of The Old Man.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Wrestling (Cumberland and Westmorland Style)\",\"author\":\"Walter Armstrong\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Sporting\",\"year\":1870,\"reason\":\"Treatise on the traditional Cumberland and Westmorland style of wrestling practised throughout the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Fors Clavigera: Letters to the Workmen and Labourers of Great Britain\",\"author\":\"John Ruskin\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Letters\",\"year\":1871,\"reason\":\"Ruskin's public letters, written from Brantwood on Coniston Water, return continually to the condition and character of the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Geology of the Neighbourhood of Kirkby Lonsdale and Kendal (Explanation of Quarter-Sheet 98 S.E.)\",\"author\":\"William Talbot Aveline; Thomas McKenny Hughes\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Geology\",\"year\":1872,\"reason\":\"Geological Survey memoir covering the south-eastern Lake District around Kendal, Sedbergh and Bowness.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Jenkinson's Practical Guide to the English Lake District\",\"author\":\"Henry Irwin Jenkinson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Guidebook\",\"year\":1872,\"reason\":\"Detailed Victorian guide to the Lakes by a Keswick-based writer, covering walks, drives and ascents.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Annales Caermoelenses: or Annals of Cartmel\",\"author\":\"James Stockdale\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1872,\"reason\":\"History of the parish of Cartmel and its priory on the southern edge of the Lake District.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Memoir and Letters of Sara Coleridge\",\"author\":\"Sara Coleridge; Edith Coleridge (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1873,\"reason\":\"Memoir of Coleridge's daughter with recollections of her Keswick childhood at Greta Hall among the Lakes.\"}\n{\"title\":\"The Geology of the Northern Part of the English Lake District (Explanation of Quarter-Sheet 101 S.E.)\",\"author\":\"John Clifton Ward\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Geology\",\"year\":1876,\"reason\":\"Geological Survey memoir devoted to the geology of the northern Lake District around Keswick.\"}\n{\"title\":\"Harriet Martineau's A