:1695,\"reason\":\"Gibson's edition of Camden's chorography carries detailed descriptions of Cumberland and Westmorland including the Lake mountains.\"}\n\n5. {\"title\":\"The Journal of George Fox\",\"author\":\"George Fox\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1694,\"reason\":\"Recounts Fox's 1652 mission through Westmorland, with sustained narrative of Firbank Fell, Kendal, Underbarrow and Swarthmoor in the Lake counties.\"}\n\n6. {\"title\":\"A Perambulation of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Thomas Denton\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian survey\",\"year\":1688,\"reason\":\"Manuscript antiquarian survey of Cumberland describing the seats, towns and scenery of the Lake District in 1687-88.\"}\n\n7. {\"title\":\"A Description of the County of Westmorland\",\"author\":\"Daniel Fleming\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian survey\",\"year\":1671,\"reason\":\"Sir Daniel Fleming's manuscript topographical description of Westmorland, including the Lake District valleys and fells.\"}\n\n8. {\"title\":\"A Miscellany of Poems, Consisting of Original Poems, Translations, Pastorals in the Cumberland Dialect, and Familiar Epistles\",\"author\":\"Josiah Relph\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1747,\"reason\":\"Posthumous collection by the Wigton poet including the earliest substantial verse in Cumberland dialect rooted in the local landscape.\"}\n\n9. {\"title\":\"The Antiquities of England and Wales\",\"author\":\"Francis Grose\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian\",\"year\":1772,\"reason\":\"Illustrated antiquarian survey with engraved views and descriptions of Cumberland and Westmorland castles, abbeys and monuments including Furness Abbey.\"}\n\n10. {\"title\":\"The Antiquities of Furness; or, An Account of the Royal Abbey of St. Mary, in the Vale of Nightshade, near Dalton in Furness\",\"author\":\"Thomas West\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian\",\"year\":1774,\"reason\":\"Pioneering account of Furness Abbey and the Furness