\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1819,\"reason\":\"Poem following a waggoner's journey over Dunmail Raise through the heart of the Lake District.\"}\n\n30. {\"title\":\"Confessions of an English Opium-Eater: Being an Extract from the Life of a Scholar\",\"author\":\"Thomas De Quincey\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1821,\"reason\":\"Autobiographical work whose later sections describe the author's life at Dove Cottage, Grasmere, among the Lake poets.\"}\n\n31. {\"title\":\"The Cumbrian Minstrel: Being a Poetical Miscellany of Legendary, Gothic, and Romantic Tales\",\"author\":\"John Stagg\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1821,\"reason\":\"Further Cumbrian legendary verse by Stagg, steeped in Lake county scenery and superstition.\"}\n\n32. {\"title\":\"History, Directory and Gazetteer of the County Palatine of Lancaster\",\"author\":\"Edward Baines\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1824,\"reason\":\"Includes substantial treatment of Furness and Lancashire North of the Sands, the south-western fringe of the Lake District.\"}\n\n33. {\"title\":\"Sir Thomas More: or, Colloquies on the Progress and Prospects of Society\",\"author\":\"Robert Southey\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Essays\",\"year\":1829,\"reason\":\"Dialogues staged around the author's Keswick home beneath Skiddaw, with recurring description of the Lake District landscape.\"}\n\n34. {\"title\":\"History, Directory and Gazetteer of the Counties of Cumberland and Westmorland, with that Part of the Lake District in Lancashire, Forming the Lordships of Furness and Cartmel\",\"author\":\"William Parson; William White\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1829,\"reason\":\"County directory whose gazetteer describes every Lake District town, valley and lake.\"}\n\n35. {\"title\":\"The Annals of Kendal: Being a Historical and Descriptive Account of Kendal and its Environs\",\"author\":\"Cornelius Nicholson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1832,\"reason\":\"History of the 'Gateway to the Lakes', the Westmorland market town of Kendal and its surroundings.\"}\n\n36. {\"title\":\"Westmorland, Cumberland, Durham, & Northumberland, Illustrated, from Original Drawings by Thomas Allom, George Pickering, &c.\",\"author\":\"Thomas Rose\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1832,\"reason\":\"Illustrated county topography with extensive letterpress on Lake District scenery.\"}\n\n37. {\"title\":\"Poems\",\"author\":\"Hartley Coleridge\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1833,\"reason\":\"Collection by Coleridge's son, a lifelong dweller in Grasmere and Rydal, containing sonnets on Lake District places and people.\"}\n\n38. {\"title\":\"Recollections of the Lakes and the Lake Poets\",\"author\":\"Thomas De Quincey\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1834,\"reason\":\"Series of reminiscences of Wordsworth, Coleridge and Southey grounded in Grasmere and Keswick life, published in Tait's Magazine from 1834.\"}\n\n39. {\"title\":\"The Lakes of England\",\"author\":\"George Tattersall\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1836,\"reason\":\"Illustrated work describing the principal English lakes and their scenery for the tourist.\"}\n\n40. {\"title\":\"The History and Antiquities of Carlisle, with an Account of the Gentlemen's Seats and Antiquities in the Vicinity\",\"author\":\"Samuel Jefferson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1838,\"reason\":\"History of the Cumberland county town and its district, a standard source for the northern Lake county.\"}\n\n41. {\"title\":\"Visits to Remarkable Places, Old Halls, Battle Fields, and Scenes Illustrative of Striking Passages in English History and Poetry\",\"author\":\"William Howitt\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Travel writing\",\"year\":1840,\"reason\":\"Includes a sustained account of a visit to Wordsworth at Rydal Mount and the Lake country.\"}\n\n42. {\"title\":\"Black's Picturesque Guide to the English Lakes\",\"author\":\"Adam and Charles Black (pub.); John Phillips (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Guidebook\",\"year\":1841,\"reason\":\"Early edition of Black's long-running Lake District guide, with geology-informed description by John Phillips.\"}\n\n43. {\"title\":\"The Recreations of Christopher North\",\"author\":\"John Wilson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Essays\",\"year\":1842,\"reason\":\"Contains 'Christopher in his Sporting Jacket' and other essays recording walking expeditions in the Lake District around the author's Windermere home.\"}\n\n44. {\"title\":\"The History and Antiquities of Allerdale Ward, above Derwent, in the County of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Samuel Jefferson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1842,\"reason\":\"Local history of the Cumberland ward containing Keswick, Borrowdale and the heart of the Lake District.\"}\n\n45. {\"title\":\"The Poetical Works of Miss Susanna Blamire, 'The Muse of Cumberland'\",\"author\":\"Susanna Blamire; Henry Lonsdale (ed.); Patrick Maxwell (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1842,\"reason\":\"First collected edition of the Cumbrian poet's songs and dialect verse rooted in the Eden valley and Lake county.\"}\n\n46. {\"title\":\"An Illustrated Itinerary of the County of Lancaster\",\"author\":\"Cyrus Redding\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Topographical description\",\"year\":1842,\"reason\":\"Itinerary covering the Furness district and the Lake District fringe of Lancashire north of the sands.\"}\n\n47. {\"title\":\"Kendal and Windermere Railway: Two Letters Re-printed from the Morning Post\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Pamphlet\",\"year\":1844,\"reason\":\"Wordsworth's celebrated protest against bringing the railway into the heart of the Lake District.\"}\n\n48. {\"title\":\"History, Gazetteer, and Directory of Cumberland, Comprising a General Survey of the County\",\"author\":\"William Mannix; William Whellan\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1847,\"reason\":\"Mid-Victorian directory with historical and topographical accounts of all the Cumberland Lake parishes.\"}\n\n49. {\"title\":\"The Homes and Haunts of the Most Eminent British Poets\",\"author\":\"William Howitt\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1847,\"reason\":\"Chapters on Wordsworth, Coleridge and Southey describe their Grasmere, Rydal and Keswick homes and the surrounding Lake scenery.\"}\n\n50. {\"title\":\"The Worthies of Westmorland; or, Notable Persons Born in that County since the Reformation\",\"author\":\"George Atkinson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1849,\"reason\":\"Biographies of Westmorland worthies prefaced by topographical account of the Lake county.\"}\n\n51. {\"title\":\"The Life and Correspondence of Robert Southey\",\"author\":\"Charles Cuthbert Southey\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1849,\"reason\":\"Life and letters of the poet laureate centred on his forty years at Greta Hall, Keswick, in the Lake District.\"}\n\n52. {\"title\":\"The Prelude; or, Growth of a Poet's Mind: An Autobiographical Poem\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1850,\"reason\":\"Autobiographical poem with celebrated books on the poet's childhood and schooldays at Hawkshead and residence at Grasmere.\"}\n\n53. {\"title\":\"Memoirs of William Wordsworth, Poet-Laureate, D.C.L.\",\"author\":\"Christopher Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1851,\"reason\":\"Official memoir by the poet's nephew, documenting his life at Grasmere and Rydal Mount in the Lake District.\"}\n\n54. {\"title\":\"The Northmen in Cumberland and Westmorland\",\"author\":\"Robert Ferguson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1856,\"reason\":\"Study of Norse settlement, place-names and dialect in the two Lake counties.\"}\n\n55. {\"title\":\"Cumberland and Westmorland, Ancient and Modern: The People, Dialect, Superstitions and Customs\",\"author\":\"Jeremiah Sullivan\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1857,\"reason\":\"Account of the people, dialect and customs of the Lake counties, ancient and modern.\"}\n\n56. {\"title\":\"The Official Illustrated Guide to the Lancaster and Carlisle, Eden Valley, and Penrith Railways\",\"author\":\"George S. Measom\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Railway guide\",\"year\":1859,\"reason\":\"Railway guide describing the approach to the Lakes over Shap and the branches to Kendal and Windermere.\"}\n\n57. {\"title\":\"A Glossary of Words and Phrases of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"William Dickinson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Dialect study\",\"year\":1859,\"reason\":\"Glossary recording the dialect spoken across the Cumberland Lake District, by the author of Cumbriana.\"}\n\n58. {\"title\":\"The History and Topography of the Counties of Cumberland and Westmorland, Comprising Their Ancient and Modern History\",\"author\":\"William Whellan\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1860,\"reason\":\"Comprehensive county history and gazetteer describing every Lake District parish, valley and town.\"}\n\n59. {\"title\":\"Tales and Legends of the English Lakes\",\"author\":\"Wilson Armistead\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Folklore\",\"year\":1863,\"reason\":\"Collection of legends and traditional tales attached to Lake District places.\"}\n\n60. {\"title\":\"The Lake Country\",\"author\":\"Elizabeth Lynn Linton\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Travel writing\",\"year\":1864,\"reason\":\"Woman novelist's descriptive tour of the Lakes, illustrated with one hundred engravings by W. J. Linton.\"}\n\n61. {\"title\":\"The Worthies of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Henry Lonsdale\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Biography\",\"year\":1867,\"reason\":\"Six-volume series of lives of eminent Cumbrians, a key source for the intellectual history of the Lake county.\"}\n\n62. {\"title\":\"Diary, Reminiscences, and Correspondence of Henry Crabb Robinson\",\"author\":\"Henry Crabb Robinson; Thomas Sadler (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Diary\",\"year\":1869,\"reason\":\"Diaries record repeated visits to the Lakes and friendships with Wordsworth, Coleridge and Southey in their Lake District homes.\"}\n\n63. {\"title\":\"The Folk-Speech of Cumberland and Some Districts Adjacent; Being Stories and Rhymes in the Dialect of that Border County\",\"author\":\"Alexander Craig Gibson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Dialect study\",\"year\":1869,\"reason\":\"Dialect stories and rhymes of Cumberland by the Coniston-based physician and author of The Old Man.\"}\n\n64. {\"title\":\"Wrestling: (Cumberland and Westmorland Style)\",\"author\":\"Walter Armstrong\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Sporting\",\"year\":1870,\"reason\":\"Treatise on the traditional Cumberland and Westmorland style of wrestling practised throughout the Lake District.\"}\n\n65. {\"title\":\"Fors Clavigera: Letters to the Workmen and Labourers of Great Britain\",\"author\":\"John Ruskin\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Letters\",\"year\":1871,\"reason\":\"Ruskin's public letters, written from Brantwood on Coniston Water, return continually to the condition and character of the Lake District.\"}\n\n66. {\"title\":\"The Geology of the Neighbourhood of Kirkby Lonsdale and Kendal (Explanation of Quarter-Sheet 98 S.E.)\",\"author\":\"William Talbot Aveline; Thomas McKenny Hughes; R. H. Tiddeman\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Geology\",\"year\":1872,\"reason\":\"Geological Survey memoir covering the south-eastern Lake District around Kendal, Sedbergh and Bowness.\"}\n\n67. {\"title\":\"Jenkinson's Practical Guide to the English Lake District\",\"author\":\"Henry Irwin Jenkinson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Guidebook\",\"year\":1872,\"reason\":\"Detailed Victorian guide to the Lakes by a Keswick-based writer, covering walks, drives and ascents.\"}\n\n68. {\"title\":\"Annales Caermoelenses: or Annals of Cartmel\",\"author\":\"James Stockdale\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Local history\",\"year\":1872,\"reason\":\"History of the parish of Cartmel and its priory on the southern edge of the Lake District.\"}\n\n69. {\"title\":\"Memoir and Letters of Sara Coleridge\",\"author\":\"Sara Coleridge; Edith Coleridge (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1873,\"reason\":\"Memoir of Coleridge's daughter with recollections of her Keswick childhood at Greta Hall among the Lakes.\"}\n\n70. {\"title\":\"The Geology of the Northern Part of the English Lake District (Explanation of Quarter-Sheet 101 S.E.)\",\"author\":\"John Clifton Ward\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Geology\",\"year\":1876,\"reason\":\"Geological Survey memoir devoted to the geology of the northern Lake District around Keswick.\"}\n\n71. {\"title\":\"Harriet Martineau's Autobiography\",\"author\":\"Harriet Martineau\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1877,\"reason\":\"Autobiography containing sustained account of the author's thirty years at Ambleside in the Lake District.\"}\n\n72. {\"title\":\"The English Lake District as Interpreted in the Poems of Wordsworth\",\"author\":\"William Knight (ed.)\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Anthology\",\"year\":1878,\"reason\":\"Anthology arranging Wordsworth's poems by the Lake District places they describe.\"}\n\n73. {\"title\":\"The English Lake District\",\"author\":\"Mountford John Byrde Baddeley; Charles Slegg Ward\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Guidebook\",\"year\":1880,\"reason\":\"First volume of the 'Thorough Guide' series, the standard late-Victorian guide to the Lakes.\"}\n\n74. {\"title\":\"Sonnets at the English Lakes\",\"author\":\"Hardwicke Drummond Rawnsley\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1881,\"reason\":\"Sonnets on Lake District scenes by the future Canon Rawnsley of Crosthwaite.\"}\n\n75. {\"title\":\"History, Topography and Directory of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"T. Bulmer and Co. (pub.)\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Directory\",\"year\":1883,\"reason\":\"Late-Victorian county directory with historical and topographical notices for all Cumberland Lake parishes.\"}\n\n76. {\"title\":\"A Flora of the English Lake District\",\"author\":\"John Gilbert Baker\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Natural history\",\"year\":1885,\"reason\":\"Systematic flora of the Lake District by a Kew botanist, the standard Victorian botanical account.\"}\n\n77. {\"title\":\"The Shadow of a Crime: A Cumbrian Romance\",\"author\":\"Hall Caine\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Novel\",\"year\":1885,\"reason\":\"Hall Caine's first novel, a historical romance set in Borrowdale and around Keswick in the seventeenth century.\"}\n\n78. {\"title\":\"Praeterita: Outlines of Scenes and Thoughts Perhaps Worthy of Memory in My Past Life\",\"author\":\"John Ruskin\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Memoir\",\"year\":1885,\"reason\":\"Ruskin's autobiography, including his childhood discovery of Keswick and later life at Brantwood, Coniston.\"}\n\n79. {\"title\":\"The Birds of Cumberland, Critically Studied, Including Some Notes on the Birds of Westmorland\",\"author\":\"Hugh Alexander Macpherson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Natural history\",\"year\":1886,\"reason\":\"Ornithological account of the Lake counties by the Carlisle naturalist.\"}\n\n80. {\"title\":\"A Son of Hagar: A Romance of Our Time\",\"author\":\"Hall Caine\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Novel\",\"year\":1886,\"reason\":\"Novel set in the Cumberland Lake country, drawing on its fell farming life and scenery.\"}\n\n81. {\"title\":\"Great Britain: Handbook for Travellers\",\"author\":\"Karl Baedeker\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Guidebook\",\"year\":1887,\"reason\":\"First edition of Baedeker's Great Britain contains a substantial self-contained section on the English Lakes.\"}\n\n82. {\"title\":\"Through the Wordsworth Country: A Companion to the Lake District\",\"author\":\"William Knight\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Guidebook\",\"year\":1887,\"reason\":\"Literary companion to the Lakes organised around Wordsworth's life and places, with photographs by Harry Goodwin.\"}\n\n83. {\"title\":\"Robert Elsmere\",\"author\":\"Mrs. Humphry Ward\",\"gender\":\"F\",\"genre\":\"Novel\",\"year\":1888,\"reason\":\"Best-selling novel largely set in the fictional 'Long Whindale', closely modelled on Long Sleddale in the Lake District.\"}\n\n84. {\"title\":\"Westmorland Church Notes: Being the Heraldry, Epitaphs, and Other Inscriptions in the Thirty-Two Ancient Parish Churches and Churchyards of that County\",\"author\":\"Edward Bellasis\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Antiquarian\",\"year\":1888,\"reason\":\"Heraldic and monumental record of all Westmorland's ancient churches, including those of the Lake District.\"}\n\n85. {\"title\":\"The Recluse\",\"author\":\"William Wordsworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Poetry\",\"year\":1888,\"reason\":\"First publication of Wordsworth's long-unprinted Home at Grasmere, his poem celebrating settlement in the Lake District vale.\"}\n\n86. {\"title\":\"A Coach-Drive at the Lakes: Windermere to Keswick\",\"author\":\"Hardwicke Drummond Rawnsley\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Travel writing\",\"year\":1890,\"reason\":\"Illustrated account of the classic coach journey from Windermere to Keswick by the Crosthwaite vicar.\"}\n\n87. {\"title\":\"A History of Cumberland\",\"author\":\"Richard Saul Ferguson\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"County history\",\"year\":1890,\"reason\":\"Popular county history of Cumberland by the leading Victorian antiquary of the Lake counties.\"}\n\n88. {\"title\":\"A Vertebrate Fauna of Lakeland, Including Cumberland and Westmorland with Lancashire North of the Sands\",\"author\":\"Hugh Alexander Macpherson; William Duckworth\",\"gender\":\"M\",\"genre\":\"Natural history\",\"year\":1892,\"reason\":\"Comprehensive vertebrate zoology of the Lake District region.\"}\n\n89. {\"title\":\"Papers and Pedigrees, Mainly Relating to Cumberland and We